<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<% content_for :description, "Tom Garrett — lead / principal developer. Architecture, real-time systems, event-driven integrations and applied AI. Director of Engineering at DepositCloud, founder of DocuDynamics." %>

<%# ── Intro ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20 pb-16 sm:px-8 sm:pt-28">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>

  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.5fr_1fr] lg:gap-20">
    <div>
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl font-display text-[2.4rem] font-semibold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-ink-950 sm:text-[3.4rem]">
        Ten years building and leading production systems
      </h1>

      <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-[1.06rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-500">
        <p>
          At <span class="font-medium text-ink-900">DepositCloud</span> — a regulated US
          rental-payments platform serving 250,000+ customers — I own the architecture across three
          applications, set the standards the team builds to, and still write the code for the
          difficult slice.
        </p>
        <p>
          I took its communications layer from problem definition to production calls on
          <span class="font-medium text-ink-900">Twilio Programmable Voice</span> in three months,
          then spent fifteen more making it survive carrier failures and out-of-order webhooks. I
          designed the bi-directional API contracts with Yardi, Entrata, RealPage and Rent Manager
          that unlock its enterprise accounts, and re-engineered CI/CD so a release takes four hours
          instead of two weeks. Outside it I've shipped three products solo — two of them AI
          pipelines on the Anthropic SDK.
        </p>
        <p>
          I design for the failure modes rather than the happy path — duplicate webhooks, state
          split across two stores, a model that is confidently wrong — and I write the trade-off
          down next to the decision. The case studies here are those write-ups, including the parts
          that went wrong.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="<%= contact[:cv] %>" download
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-ink-950 px-5 py-2.5 text-[0.92rem] font-medium text-paper transition hover:bg-ink-700">
          Download CV
          <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M10 3.5v10m0 0 3.5-3.5M10 13.5 6.5 10M4 16.5h12" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
        <a href="<%= contact[:github] %>" rel="noopener"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-ink-200 px-5 py-2.5 text-[0.92rem] font-medium text-ink-900 transition hover:border-ink-950">
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="lg:pt-3">
      <p class="eyebrow">Details</p>
      <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-[0.93rem]">
        <div><dt class="text-ink-400">Based</dt><dd class="text-ink-900"><%= contact[:location] %></dd></div>
        <div><dt class="text-ink-400">Currently</dt><dd class="text-ink-900">Director of Engineering, DepositCloud — hands-on</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="text-ink-400">Also</dt><dd class="text-ink-900">Independent developer &amp; adviser, 2024 – present</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="text-ink-400">Degree</dt><dd class="text-ink-900">HDip Computer Software Engineering, NFQ Level 8 (1.1)</dd></div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-ink-400">Links</dt>
          <dd class="space-y-1">
            <a class="link-underline block text-ink-900" href="<%= contact[:github] %>" rel="noopener"><%= contact[:github_label] %></a>
            <a class="link-underline block text-ink-900" href="<%= contact[:linkedin] %>" rel="noopener"><%= contact[:linkedin_label] %></a>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ── Technical ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
<section class="border-t border-ink-100 bg-panel">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 sm:px-8">
    <p class="eyebrow">Technical</p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <% [
           ["Languages &amp; frameworks", "Ruby on Rails, JavaScript, React, Node, Hotwire/Turbo, SQL, HTML/CSS, Tailwind."],
           ["Data &amp; infrastructure", "PostgreSQL, Redis, Solid Queue, Docker, GitHub Actions, Google Cloud Run, Cloud SQL, Memorystore, AWS."],
           ["Real-time &amp; event-driven", "WebSockets over Redis pub/sub, webhook idempotency and replay, row-level locking, TTL presence, retry and compensation design."],
           ["Applied AI", "Anthropic SDK — structured outputs, tool budgets, streaming, prompt caching, model tiering. GPT-4o vision, human-in-the-loop review gates, Claude Code."],
           ["Integrations &amp; APIs", "API contract design, bi-directional sync, developer experience. Twilio, HubSpot, Stripe, Salesforce, TrueLayer, Yardi, Entrata, RealPage, Rent Manager."],
           ["Leading engineers", "Architecture reviews, release standards, written initiative scoping, onboarding, incident reviews — eight engineers plus design and operations, while still shipping."]
         ].each do |title, body| %>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[1.08rem] font-semibold text-ink-950"><%= title.html_safe %></h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-500"><%= body %></p>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ── Experience ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
<section class="border-t border-ink-100">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 sm:px-8">
    <p class="eyebrow">Experience</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-16">
      <%
        roles = [
          {
            org: "DepositCloud",
            note: "Ireland (US market) — multi-tenant Rails SaaS managing the full US rental security-deposit lifecycle for property management companies and multifamily operators.",
            titles: [["Director of Engineering", "Jun 2024 – Present"]],
            points: [
              "Own the architecture across three applications serving 250k+ customers on multi-tenant Rails — 900+ merged PRs and 47 schema migrations against a live product in 24 months.",
              "<strong class=\"font-medium text-ink-900\">Twilio contact centre, 0→1:</strong> production calls inside three months, then fifteen months of hardening. Nine-language IVR, row-locked routing so check-and-claim is atomic, presence in Redis with TTLs beside PostgreSQL, and 28 webhook and agent-action endpoints made idempotent against a provider that retries — with compensation that rolls agent state back on a failed conference dial. ~5,000 calls a month; 100% of third-party licensing cost removed.",
              "Built a <strong class=\"font-medium text-ink-900\">bi-directional HubSpot CRM integration</strong> on top of it: call events log activity and contacts against the customer record, tickets are raised from the call itself, and both systems stay in sync.",
              "Designed and built the greenfield <strong class=\"font-medium text-ink-900\">PMS Sync &amp; Integration product</strong> — bi-directional API contracts with Yardi, Entrata, RealPage and Rent Manager, the integrations that unlock enterprise-tier accounts — plus Stripe and Salesforce across the wider platform.",
              "Re-engineered CI/CD (Docker, GitHub Actions) to cut the release cycle from two weeks to under four hours, and set the standards the team works to: feature flags with analytics on every significant release, staged rollout, SOC 2 Type I with automated scanning and penetration testing in CI.",
              "Lead eight distributed engineers plus design and operations — architecture reviews, written initiative scoping, weekly one-to-ones — while still building myself.",
              "Run remote sessions directly with US customers, turning recurring technical problems into architecture and product decisions."
            ]
          },
          {
            org: "Independent Developer &amp; Adviser",
            note: "Contract build and technical advisory for early-stage Irish companies.",
            titles: [["Contract Developer & Adviser", "2024 – Present"]],
            points: [
              "<strong class=\"font-medium text-ink-900\">WealthGuard</strong> (2025 – present) — built a wealth-management platform solo in Rails 8, now in production with 100+ high-net-worth clients. TrueLayer open banking and GPT-4o vision statement extraction into a 22-table domain model, 24 member and adviser screens, and a test-suite rebuild from 31.9% to 91.6% line coverage that surfaced a bank integration which had never once produced a record.",
              "<strong class=\"font-medium text-ink-900\">Guest Nutrition</strong> (2024 – present) — technical adviser to an Enterprise Ireland High Potential Start-Up (HPSU); ran discovery and feature-planning workshops and took the product from 0 to 1 into active industry field trials."
            ]
          },
          {
            org: "DocuDynamics",
            note: "Compliance-automation startup, built solo from customer discovery to production code.",
            titles: [["Founder & Lead Engineer", "Nov 2022 – Jun 2024"]],
            points: [
              "Built the entire v1 web application from concept to funded MVP in five months (React, Node, AWS), securing Microsoft for Startups and New Frontiers Phase 2 backing.",
              "Owned the critical pipeline — document upload → AI processing → collaboration — rebuilding the friction points found in 20+ user interviews and direct observation.",
              "Used real-time production analytics to kill low-engagement features and scale the workflows that earned their keep."
            ]
          },
          {
            org: "Penco",
            note: nil,
            titles: [["Developer & Digital Operations Manager", "Dec 2019 – Nov 2022"]],
            points: [
              "Shipped web and mobile features on a custom-built mortgage application and appraisal platform in two-week iterations, with continuous user interviews setting the backlog.",
              "Built a Salesforce CRM integration that eliminated 60% of manual data entry and increased operational capacity by 40%.",
              "Introduced Hotjar for user testing, cutting feature evaluation cycles by 70%.",
              "Featured in The Sunday Times (Business, Jul 2020) on helping Irish SMEs build data-driven operations."
            ]
          },
          {
            org: "Earlier roles",
            note: nil,
            titles: [["Engineering & design", "2016 – 2019"]],
            points: [
              "Full Stack Developer, Gambling.com Group, Dublin (Jan – Dec 2019) — build and user testing for a US-market comparison iOS app.",
              "UX Engineer, GRID Finance, Dublin (Jan 2018 – Jan 2019) — journey mapping and application interfaces for an SME lending engine.",
              "Multimedia Developer, Associated Newspapers, Dublin (Jun 2017 – Jun 2018).",
              "Audio Engineer, Cauldron Recording Studios, Dublin (Jun – Sep 2016)."
            ]
          }
        ]
      %>

      <% roles.each do |role| %>
        <article class="grid gap-6 border-t border-ink-100 pt-8 lg:grid-cols-[15rem_1fr] lg:gap-12">
          <div>
            <h2 class="font-display text-[1.3rem] font-semibold leading-tight text-ink-950"><%= role[:org].html_safe %></h2>
            <div class="mt-3 space-y-1.5">
              <% role[:titles].each do |title, period| %>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-[0.92rem] font-medium text-ink-700"><%= title.html_safe %></p>
                  <p class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] text-ink-400"><%= period %></p>
                </div>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <% if role[:note] %>
              <p class="mb-4 max-w-2xl text-[0.9rem] italic leading-relaxed text-ink-400"><%= role[:note].html_safe %></p>
            <% end %>
            <ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5">
              <% role[:points].each do |point| %>
                <li class="grid grid-cols-[0.75rem_1fr] gap-3 text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-500">
                  <span class="mt-[0.72rem] h-px w-2.5 bg-ink-300" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span><%= point.html_safe %></span>
                </li>
              <% end %>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ── Education & recognition ────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
<section class="border-t border-ink-100 bg-panel">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-14 px-6 py-20 sm:px-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Education &amp; further study</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-5">
        <% [
             ["Online Master of Science in Computer Science (OMSCS)", "Georgia Institute of Technology · online, part-time, in progress"],
             ["Professional Academy Diploma, Advanced Artificial Intelligence for Business", "UCD Professional Academy · Jul – Nov 2026, in progress — EU AI governance, responsible AI, risk and compliance"],
             ["New Frontiers, Phase 2 — Enterprise Ireland", "TU Dublin · Oct 2022 – Mar 2023"],
             ["Higher Diploma, Computer Software Engineering", "Dublin City University, NFQ Level 8 · Sep 2020 – Jun 2021, first-class honours (1.1)"],
             ["Professional Diploma, Digital Marketing", "Waterford Institute of Technology · 2018 – 2019"],
             ["BA (Hons), Digital Art", "IADT Dún Laoghaire, NFQ Level 8 · 2013 – 2017, second-class honours (2.1)"]
           ].each do |title, detail| %>
          <li>
            <p class="text-[0.98rem] font-medium text-ink-900"><%= title %></p>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-[0.86rem] text-ink-400"><%= detail %></p>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Recognition</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-5">
        <% [
             ["New Frontiers Phase 2 recipient", "TU Dublin"],
             ["Microsoft for Startups portfolio", "DocuDynamics"],
             ["The Sunday Times", "Business feature, July 2020 — on how Irish SMEs can become data-driven"]
           ].each do |title, detail| %>
          <li>
            <p class="text-[0.98rem] font-medium text-ink-900"><%= title %></p>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-[0.86rem] text-ink-400"><%= detail %></p>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-ink-100 p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Full CV</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-500">
          Two pages, covering everything above with the detail intact.
        </p>
        <a href="<%= contact[:cv] %>" download
           class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-ink-950 px-4 py-2 text-[0.88rem] font-medium text-paper transition hover:bg-ink-700">
          Download CV (PDF)
          <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M10 3.5v10m0 0 3.5-3.5M10 13.5 6.5 10M4 16.5h12" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
